[Term]
id: UBERON:0000303
name: adductor longus
def: "An adductor muscle that attaches to the hip and femur. In humans, it is a part of the adductor group of the thigh, that as the name suggests adducts the thigh. The adductor longus muscle forms the medial wall of the femoral triangle[WP, generalized]." [Wikipedia:Adductor_longus_muscle]
